.TH CERTMONGER 1 "October 25, 2026" "certmonger Manual"

.SH NAME
getcert

.SH SYNOPSIS
getcert add\-est\-ca [options]

.SH DESCRIPTION
Adds a CA configuration to \fIcertmonger\fR, which can subsequently be used to
enroll certificates using Enrollment over Secure Transport (EST), as
described in RFC 7030.  The configuration will use the bundled
\fIest\-submit\fR helper.  The \fIadd\-est\-ca\fR command is more or less a
wrapper for the \fIadd\-ca\fR command.

A first certificate is requested using the server's \fIsimpleenroll\fR
interface.  If the server requires a user name and password, the challenge
password given to \fBgetcert request\fR using its \fB\-L\fR or \fB\-l\fR
option is used as the password.  When no user name is set for the CA, a
challenge password of the form \fINAME\fR:\fIPASSWORD\fR provides both.
Renewals use the server's \fIsimplereenroll\fR interface, authenticated with
the current certificate and its private key.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
All user\-provided certificate files must be in PEM format.
.TP
\fB\-c\fR \fINAME\fR, \fB\-\-ca\fR=\fINAME\fR
The nickname to give to this CA configuration.  This same value can later be
passed in to \fIgetcert\fR's \fIrequest\fR, \fIresubmit\fR, and
\fIstart\-tracking\fR commands using the \fB\-c\fR flag.
.TP
\fB\-u\fR \fIURL\fR, \fB\-\-url\fR=\fIURL\fR
The location of the EST server, which must be an \fIhttps\fR URL.  The
\fI/.well\-known/est\fR path is appended to it if the URL does not include
it.  This option must be specified.
.TP
\fB\-i\fR \fILABEL\fR, \fB\-\-label\fR=\fILABEL\fR
The label which the server uses to tell the CA from others which it serves.
.TP
\fB\-R\fR \fIFILE\fR, \fB\-\-ca\-cert\fR=\fIFILE\fR
The location of a PEM\-formatted copy of the certificate(s) of the CA which
issued the EST server's certificate.  If this option is not given, the
system's trusted CA certificates are used to verify the server's
certificate.
.TP
\fB\-U\fR \fINAME\fR, \fB\-\-username\fR=\fINAME\fR
The user name to use for HTTP Basic authentication when enrolling.
.TP
\fB\-W\fR \fIFILE\fR, \fB\-\-password\-file\fR=\fIFILE\fR
The location of a file containing a password to use for HTTP Basic
authentication when enrolling, for requests which are not given a challenge
password.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Be verbose about errors.  Normally, the details of an error received from
the daemon will be suppressed if the client can make a diagnostic suggestion.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
getcert add\-est\-ca \-c EST \-u https://est.example.com/ \-R /etc/pki/est\-ca.pem
.TP
getcert request \-c EST \-k /etc/pki/tls/private/host.key \-f /etc/pki/tls/certs/host.crt \-G EC \-g 256 \-N CN=host.example.com \-L device1:secret

.SH BUGS
Please file tickets for any that you find at https://codeberg.org/freeipa/certmonger/issues

